|~ `::elision`, the kind of the marker of what a view left out, and the
   laws declared under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:elision
  |~~ An elision marks a part of an answer that a budget left out, and
      keeps the way back to it. A reader's context only grows, so a
      reader asks for a budget, `elide 4000` in a query or the host's
      flag, and every part left out gives way to a marker; an answer
      nobody bounded prints whole.

      It prints as a map under its tag,
      `::elision{:size 28 :read ~(!| get /trail/0/0 | drop 2)}`:
      `:size` counts the elements, the entries or the characters it
      stands for, `:read` is the query that, continued from the answer,
      reads the part left out, and `:head` holds the first characters of
      the text of a string, a doc or a quote. A failure the host prints
      is an alert, each subject it passed such a marker where the marker
      prints shorter.
      ::link~(::any/elide | doc) ::link~(::qlang/hosts | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :measuresWhatItLeftOut
        |~~ An elision holds the size of what it left out. ~~|
        ~({:s "a long line of text to leave out, which runs on long enough that its marker prints shorter than it"}
          | elide 20 | get /s | get /size | eq 98)

